goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:489:## 9. Decision Log
goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:493:| 2026-10-06 | Continue the complete goal in a fresh sibling lane from main `2208622aa8`, work the existing repo-cli backlog first, and use the installed 4.0.1 cohort for new proof. Keep merges with the fleet orchestrator as the explicit continuation handoff requires. | The prior owning worktree and private handoff files are absent; PRs #1390, #1467 and #1468 are merged and their merge commits are ancestors of this base. The original eight-suite and spawn-environment work is already landed. The frozen 4.0.1 install passes; all four installed Effect Vitest source/README files match immutable tag `460272d30457f4697d8b8c52cad41caccbcace08`. The initial detector ratchet introduces and resolves zero rows. Remaining backlog, baseline and current-cohort proof limits are in `history/2026-10-06-continuation-provenance.md`. No acceptance gate or historical finding identity is changed. | Archive the continuation lane and revert only its later commits if its work is withdrawn. Preserve the merged checkpoints, original receipt cohorts, and historical ledger IDs. Requalify the actual installed cohort after any future dependency change before reusing runtime or package evidence. |
goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:501:| 2026-10-06 | Create draft PR #1467 through REST after Yeet pushed its clean head but GitHub GraphQL PR creation failed. Keep the Heavy label pending while inherited coverage fixes #1452 and #1466 are open, and observe tier-one checks through exact-head REST until Yeet can discover the PR. | Yeet passed all pre-push gates and pushed `8799484f9ac5`. REST found no existing PR, then created #1467 at that exact SHA. Both detached and attached Yeet monitors failed for environment/discovery reasons; neither produced a merge-ready verdict. Running Heavy before the owning coverage repairs land would consume runners for a known rerun. The recurrence is recorded in `research/OPPORTUNITIES.md`. | Once the inherited fixes merge, integrate `origin/main`, add `ready-for-heavy`, and re-submit the canonical monitor. If REST created the wrong PR, close the draft and recreate it through Yeet after discovery recovers; retain the pushed source and proof. |
goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:504:| 2026-10-06 | Start the next repo-cli artifact-IO wave in a sibling worktree stacked on #1460's published head, and carry the unpushed round-three follow-up decision into that lane. Migrate the artifact tests to runner-owned MemoryFileSystem and Path layers, fix their two actionable lens findings, and correct issue #1461's exception rationale here rather than pushing a third review round to #1460. | The published #1460 Heavy run keeps its exact source fixed. In the new lane, seven artifact detector rows disappear with no introduction; all seven focused tests pass on Node and Bun, direct test-project typechecking passes, and the historical detector/lens IDs retain source evidence and a fix commit. Full `@beep/repo-cli` package verification passed (audit 838.8 seconds, docgen 24.0 seconds). The wording correction preserves its EV004 identity and acknowledges block-shared TestConsole. See `research/cli-artifacts-io-scope-proof.md`; hosted proof remains separate. | Drop this stacked branch before publication if #1460 changes the underlying source; otherwise revert the artifact source, baseline, ledger statuses, and rationale together in a follow-up PR, then rerun Node/Bun tests, typecheck, detector, and package verification. Do not move historical IDs when reversing. |
goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:509:| 2026-10-06 | Migrate `changeset-status.test.ts` to per-case `it.layer` fixtures with `MemoryFileSystem`, `Path`, `TestConsole`, and a stubbed child-process spawner. Use each `it.effect` scope for its temporary directory and a 30-second layer timeout. | The subject consumes abstract filesystem/path services and captured Git output; all 19 focused tests pass with the memory layer, and the current scanner reports zero findings in this file (eight fewer than its accepted detector ledger). This avoids the old custom scoped-layer wrapper while preserving per-case command capture and cleanup. Node/Bun focused runs and full repo-cli package audit/docgen passed on the pre-stack source `b8432779e9813d6b2b2024bf2c5516a07858f165`; the stacked source is `ebf76a2d7d13f219450b17fceb1b54a8db008c9a`. See `research/cli-changeset-status-scope-proof.md`. The follow-up baseline subtracts exactly eight rows; current-base combined `@beep/repo-cli` package verification passed (audit 704.0 seconds, docgen 25.6 seconds); hosted gates remain pending. | Revert the source, detector-ledger, and baseline changes together in a follow-up PR; restore the prior Node-backed fixture only if a platform-specific behavior is demonstrated. Preserve the original detector IDs and evidence when reversing. |
goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:516:| 2026-10-06 | Reconcile the reviewed nine-file continuation at source `bd7a8e0301` and the two inspected historical P1 metadata residues. Reuse the completed isolated baseline checkout for the after run by fast-forwarding only to that source. | The 65 selected historical IDs remain stable: 50 current fixes, six upstream fixes, nine source-bound exceptions; two current judgments are appended. FilePath severity follows the accepted review downgrade, and the verdict diagnostic row cites its actual upstream fix. Timing reuses identical installed dependencies and keeps the immutable before SHA/reports; no full-goal or speedup claim follows. | Revert source and its 65-row/baseline transition together; reverse the two P1 metadata field changes independently from their retained preimages. The timing checkout can return to `2208622aa8` after its current run stops; before reports remain retained. |
